<p>{% trans %}A Name field splits a name into parts. This helps with sorting, searching, and display.{% endtrans %}</p>

<h2>{% trans %}Core parts{% endtrans %}</h2>
<ul>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Title</strong>: A prefix like Mr., Ms., or Dr.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Given</strong>: First name.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Middle</strong>: Middle name or names.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Family</strong>: Last name or surname.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Generational</strong>: Suffix like Jr. or III.{% endtrans %}</li>
  <li>{% trans %}<strong>Credentials</strong>: Suffix like MD or PhD.{% endtrans %}</li>
</ul>

<h2>{% trans %}Extra values{% endtrans %}</h2>
<p>{% trans %}You can also use a preferred value and an alternative value. These can come from other fields and can be used in display formats.{% endtrans %}</p>

<p>{% trans %}For a long title list, see the Titles help topic.{% endtrans %}</p>
